{"id":"n-20261011-o35ixz","category":"business","display_title":"AI Growth Shakes Digital Publishers","display_title_he":"צמיחת הבינה המלאכותית מזעזעת את המוציאים לאור הדיגיטליים","short_summary":"Traditional news websites and digital advertising firms face severe financial pressures as artificial intelligence search engines and social platforms alter how users consume content.","english_level":"C1","words":432,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001558959","title":"\"אולי הגניבה הגדולה בהיסטוריה\" אתרי החדשות מאבדים גולשים ל-AI וענקיות הפרסום הדיגיטלי בלחץ","published_at":"2026-10-11T02:57:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-11T02:57:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-11T06:05:23.120Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The rapid rise of artificial intelligence and advanced search tools has triggered a profound crisis for traditional news websites and digital advertising companies across the globe. Internal correspondence from major technology firms, including OpenAI and Microsoft, recently highlighted that automated AI products present an existential threat to modern journalism. According to corporate documents revealed by industry reports, tech executives noted that utilizing human-generated information from news sites for AI models amounts to an unprecedented scale of labor appropriation.","This structural shift in media consumption has reached the Israeli legal and corporate arena with severe consequences. OpenWeb, a prominent technology enterprise that provides comment management and advertising systems for digital publishers, recently filed a request for a trustee appointment at the Tel Aviv District Court. The company faced mounting financial liabilities, including a significant debt owed to the Liquidity debt fund. Court filings demonstrated a dramatic downgrade in the firm's financial expectations, reflecting an environment where advertising revenue on traditional news portals is steadily drying up. Behind this distress lies a broader market phenomenon, as digital users abandon traditional platforms for closed, AI-driven environments that require no active browsing or article reading.","Industry analysts explain that modern web users increasingly migrate toward closed environments and conversational AI systems, such as ChatGPT, Gemini, Instagram, and TikTok. These platforms deliver concise, personalized answers directly, eliminating the necessity for users to browse traditional articles or search through open web links. Consequently, digital advertising inventory shrinks, reducing monetization opportunities for publishers and intermediaries alike. Advertisers now favor AI-saturated zones for smarter product targeting, leaving publishers with fewer intermediaries and diminishing traffic.","Prominent content recommendation giants rooted in Israel, namely Taboola and Teads, formerly known as Outbrain, have also experienced major market adjustments and substantial losses in investor value since their public market debuts. Both firms operate on revenue-sharing models tied directly to traffic within publishing networks. Recent policy alterations by major search engines and a general contraction in referral traffic have compelled these technology providers to lower financial forecasts, reduce headcounts, and navigate complex commercial disputes. For instance, Taboola faced severe stock drops after search policy changes penalized certain referral practices, while Teads reported substantial viewing declines across its partner news networks.","Market observers point out that the growing dominance of zero-click conversions allows users to satisfy their informational needs without visiting external destinations. As artificial intelligence engines expand their data capabilities and retain consumer attention longer, independent content creators and traditional news organizations continue to bear the primary financial burden of this digital transformation, while technology giants capture a larger share of user engagement and revenue."],"facts":[{"fact":"OpenAI and Microsoft correspondence revealed that AI search engines pose an existential threat to news publishers, with Microsoft describing data scraping as a massive theft of human labor.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"OpenWeb, a prominent Israeli content comment and advertising management company, filed for the appointment of a trustee due to a 60 million shekel debt to Liquidity debt fund.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"OpenWeb's financial forecasts dropped dramatically, with expected 2026 revenue falling from 257 million dollars to 110 million dollars, and its valuation dropping significantly.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Major digital content recommendation firms Taboola and Teads (formerly Outbrain) have faced billions in market value losses and declining ad traffic as users shift to AI search tools and closed social networks.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"rapid","lemma":"rapid","pos":"adjective","he":"מהיר","name":false},{"text":"rise","lemma":"rise","pos":"noun","he":"עלייה","name":false},{"text":"artificial","lemma":"artificial","pos":"adjective","he":"מלאכותי","name":false},{"text":"intelligence","lemma":"intelligence","pos":"noun","he":"בינה","name":false},{"text":"advanced","lemma":"advanced","pos":"adjective","he":"מתקדם","name":false},{"text":"search","lemma":"search","pos":"noun","he":"חיפוש","name":false},{"text":"tools","lemma":"tool","pos":"noun","he":"כלים","name":false},{"text":"triggered","lemma":"trigger","pos":"verb","he":"עורר","name":false},{"text":"profound","lemma":"profound","pos":"adjective","he":"עמוק","name":false},{"text":"crisis","lemma":"crisis","pos":"noun","he":"משבר","name":false},{"text":"traditional","lemma":"traditional","pos":"adjective","he":"מסורתי","name":false},{"text":"news","lemma":"news","pos":"noun","he":"חדשות","na